       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function, no allergies) would justify going above that. At this dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT effects, GI effects, and bleeding.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n1. **A typical dose.** For example, 50 mg once daily is the usual start for depression or anxiety. It can be titrated up to 200 mg once daily. Tell me the dose and I'll enter it.\n2. **400 mg is intended.** If it's deliberate, for example for a specific refractory indication, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I can enter it with that note so pharmacy and nursing see it's intentional. Expect pharmacy to ask for verification.\n3. **A typo.** For example, you may have meant 40 mg or 100 mg.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
